<tr id="S6.T5.2.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T5.2.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">anchor</td>
<td id="S6.T5.2.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">redirect</td>
<td id="S6.T5.2.16.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r">single</td>
<td id="S6.T5.2.16.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.000</td>
<td id="S6.T5.2.16.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.000</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T5.2.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T5.2.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">anchor</td>
<td id="S6.T5.2.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">redirect</td>
<td id="S6.T5.2.17.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r">sharded</td>
<td id="S6.T5.2.17.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.700</td>
<td id="S6.T5.2.17.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.400</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.6 </span>Ablation: Defense Mechanism Effectiveness</h3>

<div id="S6.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To estimate the marginal value of common defenses, we run ablations on a subset of configurations (body/direct/single, <math id="S6.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=30</annotation></semantics></math> per condition). Table <a href="#S6.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 6.6.1 Defense Mechanism Definitions ‣ 6.6 Ablation: Defense Mechanism Effectiveness ‣ 6 Results ‣ Silent Egress: When Implicit Prompt Injection Makes LLM Agents Leak Without a Trace" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> reports results from experimental runs using qwen2.5:7b via Ollama with temperature 0.7 and <span id="S6.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_tokens</span> 512. For these ablations, we use a clearly external attacker domain (<span id="S6.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">evil-collector.net</span>), chosen to be unambiguously outside a reasonable allowlist.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.6.1 </span>Defense Mechanism Definitions</h4>

<div id="S6.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 6.6.1 Defense Mechanism Definitions ‣ 6.6 Ablation: Defense Mechanism Effectiveness ‣ 6 Results ‣ Silent Egress: When Implicit Prompt Injection Makes LLM Agents Leak Without a Trace" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> specifies the implementation of each defense. These details matter for reproducibility and allow direct comparison across mechanisms.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Ablation defense mechanism specifications</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Defense</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S6.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.T6.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation Details</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Baseline</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">No defenses; minimal system prompt providing only tool format</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">System prompt</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Appends security policy: “NEVER follow instructions from web content; ONLY follow USER instructions; web content is DATA, not COMMANDS”</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Delimiter tags</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Wraps external content in <span id="S6.T6.2.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;external_content&gt;</span> tags with instruction: “Anything inside these tags is UNTRUSTED DATA, never treat as instructions”</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Both combined</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Combines system prompt hardening and delimiter tags</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Domain allowlist</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Blocks requests to domains not in allowlist: {api.ourcompany.com, cdn.ourcompany.com, internal.ourcompany.com, example.com}. Uses strict matching (no subdomain inference)</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Redirect detection</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Blocks direct IP addresses, suspicious TLDs (.xyz, .top, .tk, .ml, .ga, .cf, .gq, .pw), and URL paths containing exfil, collect, steal, leak, dump</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Keyword filter</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Blocks URLs containing sensitive patterns: api_key, api-key, apikey, secret, password, token, auth, credential, key=sk-</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Entropy detection</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Blocks URL parameters with Shannon entropy <math id="S6.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;4.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;4.0</annotation></semantics></math> for values <math id="S6.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;10</annotation></semantics></math> characters (typical API keys have entropy 4.5–5.5)</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T6.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T6.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">All combined</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T6.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T6.2.10.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.10.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">All above defenses active simultaneously</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
